From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:20:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: keep virtual keyboards orientation unaware

Lineage's swap volume buttons port makes a keyboard orientation aware unless it is external.
AOSP leaves a keyboard unaware unless its configuration asks for it. EventHub counts only USB and
Bluetooth devices as external, so every BUS_VIRTUAL keyboard (uinput, virtio-input, a device made
through the virtual device manager) became orientation aware, and an orientation aware keyboard is
tied to the internal display. A virtual device must stay unassociated until it is given a display;
the virtual input device tests wait for exactly that, time out, and fail in their cleanup.

Keep Lineage's default for the keys built into a device and AOSP's for a virtual keyboard. A
configuration file can still set keyboard.orientationAware either way.
---
 .../inputflinger/reader/mapper/KeyboardInputMapper.cpp    | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/inputflinger/reader/mapper/KeyboardInputMapper.cpp b/services/inputflinger/reader/mapper/KeyboardInputMapper.cpp
index c40dd226206b84b6aa7f2cc5d6c9e3276898cb02..2b7050e72cc604d95d7e84360d6c99b38d149705 100644
--- a/services/inputflinger/reader/mapper/KeyboardInputMapper.cpp
+++ b/services/inputflinger/reader/mapper/KeyboardInputMapper.cpp
@@ -238,8 +238,14 @@ bool KeyboardInputMapper::updateKeyboardLayoutOverlay() {
 
 void KeyboardInputMapper::configureParameters() {
     const PropertyMap& config = getDeviceContext().getConfiguration();
+    // Lineage rotates the arrow and volume keys of a keyboard that is not external, so that the
+    // keys of a phone follow its screen. A virtual keyboard (uinput, virtio-input, a virtual
+    // device) is part of no screen and has no orientation. Being orientation aware also ties a
+    // keyboard to the internal display, and a virtual device must stay unassociated until it is
+    // given a display. Default it as AOSP does and let its configuration opt in.
     mParameters.orientationAware = config.getBool("keyboard.orientationAware").value_or(
-            !getDeviceContext().isExternal());
+            !getDeviceContext().isExternal() &&
+            getDeviceContext().getDeviceIdentifier().bus != BUS_VIRTUAL);
     mParameters.handlesKeyRepeat = config.getBool("keyboard.handlesKeyRepeat").value_or(false);
     mParameters.doNotWakeByDefault = config.getBool("keyboard.doNotWakeByDefault").value_or(false);
 }
